Rejoin of a node by the cluster files seqno, three cases on one cluster: a node stopped cleanly catches up by IST; a node paused with SIGSTOP misses ALTER CLUSTER ADD, refuses IST on the files seqno and rejoins by full SST without a restart; a node that misses ALTER CLUSTER ADD and can not receive the added table gives up after two attempts, the cluster stays closed with the reason, the daemon keeps running. Every check of the node 3 log reads only the lines of its own case.
––– block: ../base/replication/rejoin-setup –––
––– comment –––
Clean restart: node 3 stops cleanly and misses one write; after the restart Galera takes its position from grastate.dat and asks for IST, the node accepts it: no refusal, no abort by Galera, no full SST
––– input –––
export INSTANCE=3; stdbuf -oL searchd --stopwait -c test/clt-tests/base/searchd-with-flexible-ports.conf > /dev/null; echo "stopped $?"; L3=$(wc -l < /var/log/manticore-3/searchd.log)
––– output –––
stopped 0
––– input –––
mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "INSERT INTO v1:t0 (id,title,v) VALUES (2,'b',2)"; echo $?; LC=$(mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "SHOW STATUS LIKE 'cluster_v1_last_committed'\G" | awk '/Value:/{print $2}'); echo "last_committed $LC"
––– output –––
0
last_committed 3
––– input –––
export INSTANCE=3; stdbuf -oL searchd --logreplication -c test/clt-tests/base/searchd-with-flexible-ports.conf > /dev/null; echo "started $?"
––– output –––
started 0
––– input –––
timeout 90 bash -c 'v() { mysql -h0 -P3306 -e "SHOW STATUS LIKE '\''cluster_v1_$1'\''\G" 2>/dev/null | awk "/Value:/{print \$2}"; }; until [ "$(v node_state)" = synced ] && [ "$(v last_committed)" = 3 ]; do sleep 0.5; done'; echo "synced $?"
––– output –––
synced 0
––– input –––
echo "t0 $(mysql -h0 -P3306 -N -e "SELECT id FROM t0" | grep -Eo "[0-9]+" | sort -n | xargs)"
––– output –––
t0 1 2
––– comment –––
Log of node 3 after the restart: Galera starts from the saved position 2, the donor sends IST from it and the node accepts it; no stale refusal, no abort, no full SST
––– input –––
A=$(tail -n +$((L3+1)) /var/log/manticore-3/searchd.log); chk() { echo "$A" | grep -q -- "$2" && echo "yes: $1" || echo "no: $1"; }; chk 'saved position' 'End state: [0-9a-f-]*:2 '; chk 'IST chosen' 'State gap can be likely serviced using IST'; chk 'IST join sync seqno 2' "join sync 'v1', gtid [^ ]*:2, files seqno 1, sent ok, tables 1, ist 1"; chk 'IST received' 'IST received: [0-9a-f-]*:3'; chk 'stale IST' 'stale IST request'; chk 'abort' 'Will never receive state'; echo "full SST $(echo "$A" | grep -c "join sync 'v1', .*, ist 0,")"
––– output –––
yes: saved position
yes: IST chosen
yes: IST join sync seqno 2
yes: IST received
no: stale IST
no: abort
full SST 0
––– comment –––
Missed ALTER CLUSTER ADD: node 3 is paused and misses ALTER CLUSTER ADD t1 and two writes; on resume Galera gives it IST, the donor sends CLUSTER_SYNCED with files seqno 4 (its ALTER CLUSTER ADD), node 3 has 1, refuses and rejoins by full SST without a restart
––– block: ../base/replication/rejoin-pause-node3 –––
––– input –––
L3=$(wc -l < /var/log/manticore-3/searchd.log); mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "CREATE TABLE t1 (title text, v int)"; mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "INSERT INTO t1 (id,title,v) VALUES (1,'x',1)"; timeout 60 mysql -h0 -P1306 -e "ALTER CLUSTER v1 ADD t1"; echo $?
––– output –––
0
