Evidence from the node 3 log of this case: IST refused on the files seqno, one rejoin attempt, full SST from the donor position, no crash and no restart
––– input –––
A=$(tail -n +$((L3+1)) /var/log/manticore-3/searchd.log); chk() { echo "$A" | grep -q -- "$2" && echo "yes: $1" || echo "no: $1"; }; chk 'IST chosen' 'State gap can be likely serviced using IST'; chk 'IST refused on files seqno' "files seqno 1 differs from donor files seqno 4 on IST"; chk 'rejoin attempt 1' "rejoin by SST, attempt 1 of 2"; chk 'SST join sync seqno 6' "join sync 'v1', gtid [^ ]*:6, files seqno 4, sent ok, tables 2, ist 0"; echo "crash dumps $(echo "$A" | grep -c 'CRASH DUMP') restarts $(echo "$A" | grep -c 'watchdog: main process .* forked ok')"
––– output –––
yes: IST chosen
yes: IST refused on files seqno
yes: rejoin attempt 1
yes: SST join sync seqno 6
crash dumps 0 restarts 0
––– input –––
for p in 1306 2306; do echo "$p $(mysql -h0 -P$p -e "SHOW STATUS LIKE 'cluster_v1_node_state'\G" | awk '/Value:/{print $2}')"; done
––– output –––
1306 synced
2306 synced
